oes and heat waves in the summer, and ice storms and blizzards in the winter.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn7le17ob10re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Are you saying that the weather is becoming more extreme?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Brock Tameland</span>: Absolutely. The current patterns have become impossible to predict. The data that was collected by our colleagues 20 years ago is now obsolete. because which should not be there. The scientists who first studied climate change never imagined that things would get so bad in such a short amount of time.", "id": 2, "time": "30000", "image": "engenn7le17ob10re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: This seems to be a problem which people keep ignoring, though.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Brock Tameland</span>: I agree. Many books were published by world-renowned authors on the subject. Even Hollywood is playing its part by releasing blockbusters that are raising awareness on this issue.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I think some of those movies were even made by the same director! Maybe it's someone who's as concerned about natural disasters as you are!", "id": 3, "time": "53000", "image": "engenn7le17ob10re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Environmental News"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Natural Disasters"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>When you want to clarify which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.</p><p>You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.</p><p>In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>, rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.</p><p>You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example:</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">The man who called wanted to speak to Tom.</span><br/>Which man? The man who called.<br/>The clause <span class=\"italic\">who called</span> immediately follows man - the noun it describes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example:</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">Can you return the book that I lent you?</span><br/>Which book? The book I lent you."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Relative Pronoun </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Type of Relative Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The data which was collected by our colleagues 20 years ago is now obsolete.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which was collected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The scientists who first studied climate change never imagined that things would get so bad.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who first studied the climate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Hollywood is playing its part by releasing blockbusters that are raising awareness on this issue.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that are raising awareness\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past Passive"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you are writing a news article or giving an interview, you can include the Simple Past Passive to describe something done by someone at sometime in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a regular sentence structure, you use Subject + verb + object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Many concerned locals showed me the negative effects of climate change.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the Simple Past Passive form, you use the structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Object + <span class=\"italic\">was</span> / <span class=\"italic\">were</span> + past participle + <span class=\"italic\">by</span> Subject</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I was shown the negative effect of climate change by many concerned locals.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many books were published by world-renowned authors on the subject."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think some of those movies were even made by the same director!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "globally"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "involving the entire world"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Natural disasters have increased globally."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about extreme weather."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pollutant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a toxic substance released into the atmosphere or in the water"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Pollutants pose a threat to our freshwater lakes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "saturated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "loaded to full capacity; thoroughly impregnated"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Freshwater lakes are becoming saturated with pollutants."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tornado"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "violently rotating winds resembling a funnel-shaped cloud"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: tornadoes are affecting many areas in the summer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heat wave"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a prolonged period of unusually hot weather"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The situation is made even worse by heat waves in the summer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ice storm"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a storm of freezing rain that leaves a coating of ice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ice storms cause many problems in the winter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blizzard"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a severe snowstorm"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Blizzards affect many areas in North America in the winter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob10aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "obsolete"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "out of date, no longer relevant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The data that which was collected by our colleagues 20 years ago is now obsolete."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob10aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le17ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a news story about a natural disaster that happened in your country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Past Passive to make sentences (10 to 12 sentences)  for your news story. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange stories with a partner and edit each other's stories focusing on the correct use of the Past Passive."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with a partner and compare stories."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I  write about natural disasters."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I  talk about past experiences and international news."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I  edit another person's work."}]}], "type": "sena"}